\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Remark}
\title{Whitney forms on a smooth triangulation}
\date{2026-11-15}

\p{Over #{\mathbb R}, let the manifold be compact, oriented and
Riemannian, with a smooth triangulation and the relative
boundary conditions of the paper. Write #{\eta_n} for the mesh
of the standard subdivision.}

\p{The Whitney map sends a real cochain to an #{\mathrm L^2}
form. It intertwines the simplicial coboundary with the exterior
derivative,
##{W\,\mathrm d\,c=\mathrm d\,Wc,}
by \citet{(1.4), p. 82}{dodziuk1976hodge}.
Integrating that form over a simplicial chain recovers the
pairing of the cochain with the chain, by
\citet{(1.7), p. 84}{dodziuk1976hodge}.}

\p{\citet{Theorem 3.7, p. 89}{dodziuk1976hodge}
states a pointwise bound. For a smooth #{q}-form #{f} there is a
constant #{C_f}, independent of the subdivision, such that
##{\|f(p)-W_n R_n f(p)\|_p\le C_f\eta_n}
almost everywhere.}

\p{\citet{Definition 4.1, p. 93}{dodziuk1976hodge}
sets the inner product of two cochains equal to the #{\mathrm L^2}
inner product of their Whitney forms. For a smooth form whose
de Rham image lies in the relative cochains,
\citet{Theorem 4.9, p. 95}{dodziuk1976hodge}
sends the three summands of the combinatorial Hodge
decomposition to the three summands of the smooth Hodge
decomposition, with convergence in #{\mathrm L^2}.}

\p{\citet{Theorem 5.7, p. 99}{dodziuk1976hodge}
compares eigenvalues of the Laplacian on functions. For each
positive integer #{i} at most the dimension of the finite function
space,
##{\lambda_i^{(n)}-C_i\eta_n\le\lambda_i\le\lambda_i^{(n)}.}
The constant #{C_i} depends on the index and not on the
subdivision.}
